.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap30/review_prompt1.txt
Review the uncommitted AutoEDA stmap30 iteration in this ABC repository.

Binding context:
- Project family: stmap
- New command: stmap30
- Required policy: preserve stmap0 through stmap29, keep map behavior unchanged, expose new behavior only through stmap30.
- Evaluation contract: build, stmap30 -h, smoke, all four benchmark flows, parseable final stime metrics, CEC for all four benchmarks, and runtime logs under .autoeda/runtime/results/stmap30.

Implementation summary:
- Added src/base/abci/abcStmap_30.c, registered stmap30 in src/base/abci/abc.c, added it to src/base/abci/module.make and abclib.dsp.
- stmap30 passes fSkipFanout=31 to Abc_NtkMap.
- mapperMatch.c extends the existing stmap29 continuous moderate-seed penalty with a smaller continuous penalty for high-reference strong deep seeds in the same middle-slack band.
- mapperInt.h and mapperCore.c add stmap30 counters and diagnostics for moderate and strong penalty seeds/blocks.

Validation already run:
- make ABC_USE_NO_READLINE=1 passed; log .autoeda/runtime/results/stmap30/build.log
- ./abc -c "stmap30 -h" passed; log .autoeda/runtime/results/stmap30/help.log
- Smoke flow on benchmarks/i10.aig passed; log .autoeda/runtime/results/stmap30/smoke_i10.log
- Full baseline/candidate evaluation passed for benchmarks/i10.aig, benchmarks/ode.abc.blif, benchmarks/or1200.abc.blif, benchmarks/syn2.abc.blif; artifacts include metrics.csv, comparison.csv, summary.json, guard_stats.csv, penalty_stats.csv, relief_diag.csv, near_miss_diag.csv, moderate_penalty_block_diag.csv, strong_penalty_block_diag.csv.
- CEC passed for all four benchmarks; see cec_summary.json.

Please review for correctness issues, especially:
- command registration/build integration errors,
- mode-number or range mistakes that alter stmap0-stmap29 behavior,
- uninitialized counters or diagnostics,
- incorrect stmap30 gating that changes non-stmap30 paths,
- evaluation/logging completeness problems that should block counting this iteration.

Return prioritized findings with file/line references. If there are no blocking findings, say so explicitly.
