   598	/**Function*************************************************************
   599	
   600	  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if a fanout/load proxy should reject this cut.]
   601	
   602	  Description [Mode 1 is the classic map -f guard. Mode 2 is the stmap1
   603	  selective guard, which only rejects wider cuts when the node has higher
   604	  estimated fanout. Mode 3 is the stmap2 guard, which uses the same fanout
   605	  thresholds only during area recovery and only when the current phase has
   606	  slack over the mapper required time. Mode 4 is the stmap3 guard, which
   607	  narrows the intervention to high-fanout nodes with only shallow positive
   608	  slack. Mode 5 is the stmap4 split-phase guard: stmap1-style guarding in
   609	  delay matching and stmap2-style slack-aware guarding in area recovery.
   610	  Mode 6 is the stmap5 shape-gated split-phase guard: the delay pass only
   611	  uses stmap1-style guarding in very large mapper graphs, while area recovery
   612	  keeps the stmap2 slack-aware guard. Mode 7 is the stmap6 area-sensitive
   613	  shape-gated guard: the delay pass keeps the stmap5 graph-size gate, small
   614	  mapper graphs keep the stmap2 slack-aware recovery guard, and exact-area
   615	  recovery on larger graphs checks the cut after matching so materially cheaper
   616	  cuts can override the fanout/load proxy. Mode 8 is the stmap7 criticality-
   617	  sensitive version of mode 7: exact-area recovery on larger graphs allows the
   618	  override only with deeper mapper slack and outside the highest fanout bucket.
   619	  Mode 9 is the stmap8 arrival-bounded version of mode 8: the area-saving
   620	  override also requires the candidate match to stay within one quarter of an
---
   860	  arrival gain. In stmap22, the same deep-seed path is relaxed to a moderate
   861	  mapper-arrival gain. In stmap23, moderate deep seeds also need near-critical
   862	  existing mapper slack. In stmap24, the moderate deep slack gate is tightened
   863	  to the lower edge of the critical slack window. In stmap25, the stmap24 rule
   864	  is kept, and one moderate deep seed from the next slack band is admitted for
   865	  ablation. In stmap26, the first such moderate seed is skipped and only the
   866	  second qualifying seed is admitted. In stmap27, moderate deep candidates in
   867	  the next slack band are admitted unless they match the high-reference,
   868	  low-slack, stronger-moderate signature isolated by stmap26. In stmap28, that
   869	  hard blocker is replaced by a soft area-margin penalty on high-reference
   870	  moderate seeds whose slack and arrival-gain ratios resemble load-risky
   871	  choices. In stmap29, the high-reference penalty is made continuous over the
   872	  same seed band. In stmap30, the same load-risk surface is extended to
   873	  high-reference strong deep seeds with a smaller continuous penalty.]
   874	
   875	  SideEffects []
   876	
   877	  SeeAlso     []
